<title>USA: USDA to buy up to $12 mln worth of Alaska salmon.</title>
<headline>USDA to buy up to $12 mln worth of Alaska salmon.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday said it would buy up to $12 million worth of Alaska salmon for the school lunch program and other domestic feeding programs to help ease a market glut.</p>
<p>USDA said the Alaska salmon industry, beleaguered by record-large harvests over the last several years, faces another large harvest for the 1997 season.</p>
<p>USDA also said it will continue working with the industry to develop strategies to expand market outlets.</p>
<p>Alaska Governor Tony Knowles announced Wednesday that USDA would buy surplus Alaska salmon.</p>
</text>
